 "summary": "The negative-twist Euler number statement is faithful: `signedPointTwistCore \u2026 false` glues by `pointTwistCoord` so its sections are sections of `L` vanishing at `x`, `pointTwistDiv` vanishes exactly at `x`, and the local index there is `sign |g x|\u00b2 = 1`, giving `\u27e8e(L(-x)), [X]\u27e9 = \u27e8e(L), [X]\u27e9 - 1`. The witness-section hypothesis is the same as main's positive-twist theorem, can be satisfied, and no new predicates or placeholders are introduced.",
